-    else
-      m_normals.emplace_back(DoublePoint(m_normals[len - 2]));
-
-    // Karaza: a curve sampled every few microns has thousands of almost flat concave corners
-    // (rounding to whole nanometres makes it zigzag). Each one gets a spike back to the vertex,
-    // as long as the offset, and the union that cleans them up goes quadratic: 0.5 s for one
-    // 10k point shrink on 3DBenchy. Clipper2 leaves that point out at flat corners (#405); we do
